In instrumentation/clickhouse/clickhouse-client-v1-0.5/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/clickhouse/clientv1/v0_5/ClickHouseErrorCodeExtractor.java, inline the ClickHouseException extraction into getErrorType() so the zero comparison is on the integer code before converting it to a string. Use this method shape:

```java
@Nullable
static String getErrorType(@Nullable Throwable error) {
  if (error instanceof ClickHouseException) {
    int errorCode = ((ClickHouseException) error).getErrorCode();
    return errorCode == 0 ? null : Integer.toString(errorCode);
  }
  return null;
}
```

Keep the separate getErrorCode() method and its status callback wiring unchanged: response-status capture must still include "0". Preserve null/non-ClickHouse handling and all existing nonzero code results. Do not introduce integer parsing, a new helper or another abstraction. No telemetry or classification behavior changes, unrelated edits, new PR, branch/base/state changes, restacking, configuration, changelog, or replies/resolutions to review threads.

Preserve the existing ClickHouseErrorCodeExtractorTest expectations, especially zero status with null error type and client/server codes. Run the module's narrowest spotlessApply directly before its focused extraction unit tests; do not run spotlessCheck first, clean, force reruns, or weaken assertions. Report exact validation results or concrete execution blockers.

